error[TY001]: `upper` expects Str for `s` but was given Num
  --> stdlib-types.lm:13:13
   |
13 | print(upper(1))
   |             ^ expected Str
   |
   = note: the parameter is declared as `s: Str`

error[TY001]: `padStart` expects Num for `width` but was given Str
  --> stdlib-types.lm:17:22
   |
17 | print("abc".padStart("x"))
   |                      ^^^ expected Num
   |
   = note: the parameter is declared as `width: Num`

error[TY001]: `take` expects Num for `n` but was given Str
  --> stdlib-types.lm:18:19
   |
18 | print([1, 2].take("two"))
   |                   ^^^^^ expected Num
   |
   = note: the parameter is declared as `n: Num`

error[TY001]: `get` expects Str for `key` but was given Num
  --> stdlib-types.lm:19:18
   |
19 | print({a: 1}.get(1))
   |                  ^ expected Str
   |
   = note: the parameter is declared as `key: Str`

